<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>SYT.NPKTools</PackageId>
    <Title>SYT NPKTools</Title>
    <Description>Fertilizer nutrient management for .NET, with zero dependencies. Works out how much of each fertilizer to use to hit a target PPM profile by solving the mix as a linear program, and calculates the PPM of a given mixture. Ships a curated catalogue of 34 fertilizers and 22 blending scenarios, a target-string parser, and a fully managed simplex solver with no native dependencies — so the whole pipeline also runs under WebAssembly.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    No PackageReference here, deliberately: this package has no dependencies.

    The obvious candidate would be Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions, to provide
    an AddNpkTools() extension on IServiceCollection. It is not worth it. IServiceCollection belongs
    to the consuming application, which already has it, so registering these services is one line
    each against the NpkTools factory — and passing a solver explicitly is clearer than the
    registration-order rule a TryAdd-based helper would impose.
  -->

  <!--
    The unit tests exercise two internal helpers directly: ThrowIf's guard clauses, and
    ReportFormatter's culture handling — the latter is the regression test for a shipped bug, so it
    asserts on the formatter itself rather than only through the public report methods.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="SYT.NPKTools.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
